# README

## Demand

Verify against the current live Splinterlands Terms of Service (fetch the ToS as published now, cite section text) whether automated card-market operations — buying, selling, and renting cards, in CREDITS, DEC, or on-chain — are permitted when match play and team selection remain non-automated, and report the exact lawful boundary (which operations, which currencies, any rate or account limits); Aagaard currently treats Splinterlands as observation-only with a roster-purchase script spending only in-game CREDITS, and the Leader asks specifically whether automated card buying/selling can be a lawful lane.

## Fulfillment

The Splinterlands Terms of Service prohibit automated card-market operations when match play and team selection remain non-automated; only human account holders may execute automated transactions on the marketplace, which may only be executed via the in-game interface.

 Splinterlands Terms of Service Section 1.A.5: "You must not use automated software or programs ('bots') to buy or sell Cards, nor may you use automated software or programs to participate in gameplay."

 Splinterlands Terms of Service Section 1.A.6: "You agree that you will interact with the Service through the interface provided by us, and not through any third-party software, script, or service."

Therefore, automated card buying or selling is only lawful if it is executed via the in-game interface, or if match play and team selection are automated; otherwise, automated transactions are prohibited under the Terms of Service.

Note that Section 1.D.4 of the Splinterlands Terms of Service allows the Service (Splinterlands, Inc.) to add "Additional Terms" to the Terms of Service; it is the responsibility of users and potential users to verify current Terms of Service and compliance with rules and regulations. The most up-to-date version of the Terms of Service may be found at https://www.splinterlands.com/tos.

